{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He shall come down</b> — from his palace to the courthouse, or 'come down' refers back to the judgment he mentioned, 'he shall judge your poor,' in the manner of 'it shall drop as the rain' (Deuteronomy 32:2)." "<b>And the word 'גז' ( fleece)</b> — a doubled-form root [binyan pilpel] from the stem לגזוז, 'the king's fleeces.'" "<b>זרזיף</b> — a four-letter word with no parallel. Its meaning: saturated or satiation."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:59.351412142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}